# ACT ONE

= Mara finds the film that shouldn't exist.

FADE IN:

EXT. ABANDONED CINEMA - NIGHT #1#

Rain hammers a broken marquee. The letters read "TH  L ST R EL".

MARA (30s, soaked, stubborn) forces the side door with a crowbar. [[Should she have a flashlight?]]

INT. PROJECTION BOOTH - CONTINUOUS #2#

Dust. A single film canister sits on the projector, *perfectly clean*.

MARA
(whispering)
Somebody was here.

JONAH (O.S.)
Somebody still is.

She spins. JONAH (60s) steps out of the dark, holding a candle.

MARA
Who are you?

JONAH
The projectionist. Forty years, every night. Nobody comes anymore, but the film still has to run.

MARA
That's insane.

JONAH ^
That's the job.

/* Cut this beat?
MARA
Fine.
*/

He threads the film. The projector _clatters_ to life.

CUT TO:

INT. AUDITORIUM - CONTINUOUS #3#

On the screen: MARA, sitting in this exact seat, watching herself.

~I've seen this picture before,
~the ending's always the same.

>THE END<
